main.c: the refusal to run as uid 0, off inside a domain (PGSU_DOMAIN set).

A domain's identity is the one its runtime reports for the host service, uid 0; there
is no privilege behind it to drop, and check_root would otherwise end every run at
its first line. The environment variable keeps the check for a native build of the
same tree.

--- a/src/backend/main/main.c
+++ b/src/backend/main/main.c
@@ -381,7 +381,10 @@
 check_root(const char *progname)
 {
 #ifndef WIN32
-	if (geteuid() == 0)
+	/* capstone: a domain has no user of its own; the identity its runtime
+	 * reports is the host service's, uid 0, and there is no privilege behind
+	 * it to drop. The refusal below would stop every run at this line. */
+	if (geteuid() == 0 && getenv("PGSU_DOMAIN") == NULL)
 	{
 		write_stderr("\"root\" execution of the PostgreSQL server is not permitted.\n"
 					 "The server must be started under an unprivileged user ID to prevent\n"
